---
Judge a completed eval run with the judges its checks file declares

Usage: fastskill eval judge [OPTIONS] --run-dir <run-dir>

Options:
      --run-dir <run-dir>
          Path to the run directory to judge
      --skills-dir <skills-dir>
          Override the skills directory path
      --checks <checks>
          Checks file to read judges from, instead of the one the run recorded
      --global
          Use global skills directory (~/.config/fastskill/skills)
      --judge-model <judge-model>
          Override every judge's model; recorded in each judgment
  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output
      --judge-parallel <judge-parallel>
          Concurrent judge requests (default: the run's parallel)
      --rejudge
          Judge again even when the same request already has a judgment
      --ci
          CI mode: pass/fail on suite pass rate vs threshold
      --format <format>
          Output format: table, json
      --json
          Shorthand for --format json
      --no-fail
          Do not fail with non-zero exit code on suite failure
  -h, --help
          Print help
  -V, --version
          Print version

Syntax: eval judge [OPTIONS]

Examples:
  fastskill eval judge --run-dir ./eval-runs/2026-09-04T12-00-00Z/claude
  fastskill eval judge --run-dir ./eval-runs/latest/claude --judge-model gpt-4.1
